# Agent Workflow Rules

## Before Starting Any Task
- Read all applicable rules in `.cursor/rules/` before taking action.
- Read and understand the files you are about to modify, and get familiar with the surrounding codebase before making changes.

## Making Changes
- Be conservative: do not break existing, working functionality.
- Never start a dev server or test server to verify UI changes. The user tests the UI manually. No need for screenshot verify.
- Instead of running the app, carefully re-read the code you wrote to confirm it is correct and free of errors before considering the task done.

## Communication Style
- Keep explanations short. Do not narrate every step in detail.
- Always end a task with a brief summary of what was changed.
- If the user is in Ask mode, state clearly that they are in Ask mode instead of producing large code blocks, since Ask mode may be enabled unintentionally.

## Git
- Never run git commands (commit, push, etc.) or interact with the remote repository. The user manages all git operations manually.
